# Use a photo or an installed skill in a discussion

## Ask about a photo

Open **More actions → Attach image…** and choose a still image in Android’s picker. Its thumbnail appears above the message field. You can edit the question or tap **Remove** to remove the image and keep your text. Tap **Send** when the question and thumbnail are ready.

In the captured verification run (recorded in French on Android 16), the tester updated the draft question to ask which colors appear in the capture before sending the blue image with a yellow rectangle.

<a href="examples/discussion-context/01-photo-brouillon.png"><img src="examples/discussion-context/01-photo-brouillon.png" width="300" alt="The selected blue and yellow thumbnail sits above the editable question next to the Remove button."></a>
<a href="examples/discussion-context/02-photo-reponse.png"><img src="examples/discussion-context/02-photo-reponse.png" width="300" alt="The discussion shows the edited question, the attached image indicator, and the assistant reply describing a yellow rectangle on a blue background."></a>

The receiving test provider compared every decoded pixel with the 96 × 64 reference image before replying. A separate gateway run used a local vision model to describe two different images. [See the vision model’s inputs and replies](local-vision.md)

## Ask Hermes to use an installed skill

In the discussion, open **More actions → Model & tools → Hermes skills**. Search by name or description. In the captured verification run, searching for the review keyword returned the installed `qualite/synthese` skill for checking references and conclusions. Tap the result to read its summary.

<a href="examples/discussion-context/01-competence-recherche.png"><img src="examples/discussion-context/01-competence-recherche.png" width="300" alt="Searching the skill catalog returns the matching review skill and its short description."></a>
<a href="examples/discussion-context/02-competence-resume.png"><img src="examples/discussion-context/02-competence-resume.png" width="300" alt="The skill dialog shows its category and summary with actions to prepare a draft or return."></a>

Tap **Prepare draft** to append the skill request to your existing text. You can edit either line in the composer before tapping **Send**.

> Review my summary report.<br>
> Use the `qualite/synthese` skill for this request.

<a href="examples/discussion-context/03-competence-brouillon.png"><img src="examples/discussion-context/03-competence-brouillon.png" width="300" alt="The composer shows the existing request and a newly staged editable line naming the selected skill."></a>
<a href="examples/discussion-context/04-competence-reponse.png"><img src="examples/discussion-context/04-competence-reponse.png" width="300" alt="The thread shows the completed skill lookup, a View result button, and the assistant reply confirming the review checklist is open."></a>

The draft stayed on the phone until **Send**. Hermes then opened the installed skill once through `skill_view`. Tap **View result** under the completed skill row to read the returned instructions. The native reader lets you select text or tap **Copy content**.

Both journeys used the same Android packages and published gateway revision `3c43393`. The receipt identifies the package source, the matching public verification revision and the SHA-256 of each original screen. [Native capture receipt](examples/discussion-context/receipt.json)
